# Cybersecurity Notes Vault — Project Hints

## Project
- Obsidian vault for cybersecurity notes; publicly shared on GitHub (repo: ErtugrulSefal/cyber-security-notes).
- Read `@README.md` for the index, architecture, and status-tag reference.

## Architecture (HTB Academy 3-domain model)
- Flat domains at the repo root:
  - `General/` (cross-cutting fundamentals: Cryptography, Networking)
  - `Defensive_Security/`
  - `Offensive_Security/` (with subfolders: Reconnaissance, Web_Pentesting, etc.)
  - `Tools/` (cross-cutting, top-level)
  - `Templates/` (tracked in git)
- Every domain folder has an index MOC: `0_<Topic>_MOC.md`.
- Topics with multiple notes are split into subfolders; atomic notes stay in the domain folder.

## Conventions
- **Metadata**: NO YAML frontmatter. Use an HTML `<details>` + `<dl>/<dt>/<dd>` block directly under the title for all notes and MOCs.
- **Dates**: ISO format `YYYY-MM-DD` (via Templater).
- **Naming**: snake_case file/folder names; `0_<Topic>_MOC.md` for MOCs. Watch spelling — no typos like "Peneration", "Knowladge", "Challange".
- **Language**: All vault content in English.
- **Tags**: MOCs use `#MOC #<topic>`; notes use `#cybersecurity #note`; status tags `status/wip` | `status/done` | `status/review` | `status/active`.
- **Contents**: Notes may include an optional question-based `## Contents` outline under the metadata block, linking each question to its section heading via anchor links.

## Workflow
- After any batch of edits, run the audit checklist (see below) before committing.
- Commit after each important change so changes can be rolled back safely.

## Audit checklist (before commit)
- [ ] No broken relative links (verify with `git grep`/link checks)
- [ ] Every note/MOC has a `<details>` metadata block
- [ ] No YAML frontmatter (`---`) at the top of any file
- [ ] Names/spelling consistent; MOCs follow `0_<Topic>_MOC.md`
- [ ] Only English content (except proper names)

## Maintenance
- If the vault structure or conventions change, proactively suggest updating this `.goosehints` file.
- If a repeated workflow emerges, proactively suggest creating a skill or recipe instead of duplicating prompts.

## Interaction
- Make changes only with my approval; confirm before destructive or irreversible actions.